1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,970
Describe what should happen.

2
00:00:01,970 --> 00:00:03,137
Show what happened.

3
00:00:03,137 --> 00:00:04,672
Prove whether they match.

4
00:00:04,672 --> 00:00:10,937
Reality Compiler turns physical procedures into inspectable requirements and evidence-backed verdicts.

5
00:00:12,140 --> 00:00:15,236
The block must enter the marked region before the cup.

6
00:00:15,236 --> 00:00:17,930
Muse Wonder compiled this original instruction.

7
00:00:17,930 --> 00:00:25,097
Independent semantic validation checks its meaning: typed predicates, object identities, and an explicit ordering constraint.

8
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:29,083
Select the objects and region in frame zero.

9
00:00:29,083 --> 00:00:33,573
This earlier application screenshot shows selection on generated input.

10
00:00:34,770 --> 00:00:40,164
These are actual captured SAM masks and tracks on generated footage, reviewed offline.

11
00:00:40,164 --> 00:00:44,554
Deterministic geometry converts tracks into region-entry observations.

12
00:00:44,554 --> 00:00:47,502
This demonstration makes no new model requests.

13
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:50,599
The original procedure passes.

14
00:00:50,599 --> 00:00:54,714
Both entries have evidence intervals, and the block enters first.

15
00:00:54,714 --> 00:00:57,942
Click a timestamp to inspect its supporting frames.

16
00:00:57,942 --> 00:01:01,297
Confidence alone cannot establish the required order.

17
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:07,376
New uploads also map normalized evidence to original decoded source frames.

18
00:01:07,376 --> 00:01:11,341
This separate generated-input run uses local OpenCV, not SAM.

19
00:01:11,341 --> 00:01:15,112
The older Meta capture correctly remains labeled unmapped.

20
00:01:16,310 --> 00:01:19,469
Now enter a new procedure: cup before block.

21
00:01:19,469 --> 00:01:22,556
It compiles independently with local rules.

22
00:01:22,556 --> 00:01:24,494
Evaluate the same evidence.

23
00:01:24,494 --> 00:01:27,437
No tracking or visual model is run again.

24
00:01:29,310 --> 00:01:30,241
Same recording.

25
00:01:30,241 --> 00:01:31,544
Opposite requirement.

26
00:01:31,544 --> 00:01:36,135
The revision fails because the saved observations prove the reverse order.

27
00:01:36,135 --> 00:01:43,022
Side-by-side checks explain the contradiction, while matching perception fingerprints establish evidence reuse.

28
00:01:44,220 --> 00:01:46,044
Add a sterile-cup requirement.

29
00:01:46,044 --> 00:01:50,604
The visible order still holds, but these pixels cannot establish sterility.

30
00:01:50,604 --> 00:01:52,367
The actual result is unknown.

31
00:01:52,367 --> 00:01:57,657
Unsupported requirements stay explicit instead of disappearing into a confident answer.

32
00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:03,133
Original Wonder compilation and SAM tracking retain separate provenance.

33
00:02:03,133 --> 00:02:04,557
New revisions are local.

34
00:02:04,557 --> 00:02:11,917
Spark supports bounded final-state interpretation in other captured runs; it did not contribute to this ordering comparison.

35
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:19,118
For robotics and procedure review, inspect the proof, change the requirement, and check again.

36
00:02:19,118 --> 00:02:24,542
Reality Compiler: reusable evidence for independently verifiable physical procedures.
